            "review_title": "Review at Tib Chay",
            "review_text": "h4rrington\nBristol, United Kingdom13 contributions\n1\nHorrific\nFeb 2018 • Friends\nWe booked a table for 9 at 8.30 pm and were waiting outside of the restaurant for the last couple of our friends to arrive at 8.25 pm and the manager came out twice to tell us to come inside because they wanted to close the kitchen. Once inside, the manager rushed everyone for their orders - I do understand it was just before the ter holiday so the employees wanted to get home to their families, but it was quite an extreme attitude nonetheless. My friends and I ordered then everyone else’s dishes arrived (at different times) so I waited for my eggplant dish to ảive. 20 mind after the fist dish arrived, I asked after mine and was told by the manager that they were out of eggplant so I told them it was ok and I no longer want the eggplant as there’s enough food already so we can just cancel the order. 5 mins later they bring out the eggplant and emphasise how they had worked to prepare the eggplant for me. So I told them I had already cancelled the order, to which the manager replied that they had already cooked it so we must accept and pay for it, despite them not having eggplant, then me cancelling the order, then them presenting the eggplant and requiring us to take responsibility for it. \n\nIt’s such an unpleasant experience, I’m so sorry that it happened. I really hope the customer service can improve and that no-one else will have an experience like this.\nRead more\nWritten August 20, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
